{"id":"01a0657e-133c-7ee6-bd14-ec93931be771","chapterSlug":"rw8-24","paragraph":3,"wording":"[Baron]","event":"named"}
{"id":"01a0657e-133c-7417-8911-82519a7594c4","chapterSlug":"rw8-41","paragraph":276,"wording":"[Baron]","event":"named","holderSlug":"baron-regalius","holderQuote":"“That was a most impressive display, Miss! Dame Knights, Miss Runner, the splendid lance-arrows of Ailendamus be with you. I greet you on this splendid day, as Baron Regalius du Ecte, [Regent] of the Barony Veilau! Might I detain you for the slightest word?”"}
{"id":"01a0657e-133c-74df-8961-56174dd5cea4","chapterSlug":"rw8-41","paragraph":311,"wording":"[Baron]","event":"named","holderSlug":"baron-regalius","holderQuote":"“…We are unsure, Baron Regalius.”"}
{"id":"01a0657e-133c-720f-b1d4-06e17c0c7b9d","chapterSlug":"rw8-41","paragraph":410,"wording":"[Baron]","event":"named","holderSlug":"baron-regalius","holderQuote":"“Do people starve in Ailendamus, Baron Regalius? Do you have [Farmers], a lower class?”"}
{"id":"01a0657e-133c-7087-8a7d-0dfdc53f39c0","chapterSlug":"rw8-41","paragraph":421,"wording":"[Baron]","event":"named","holderSlug":"baron-regalius","holderQuote":"“Of course, thank you, Baron Regalius.”"}
{"id":"01a0657e-133c-795f-9598-4d1164d9c6ae","chapterSlug":"rw8-50","paragraph":898,"wording":"[Baron]","event":"named","holderQuote":"A fixed figure in the palace’s courts, Baron Regalius, smiled, and got a weak one from the Wind Runner. Relieved, Ryoka slowed down."}
{"id":"01a0657e-133c-71cc-8f1e-5d739c4fd825","chapterSlug":"rw8-36 H","paragraph":77,"wording":"[Baron]","event":"named","holderSlug":"baron-regalius","holderQuote":"They were grand words. Perhaps…too grand for a mere [Baron], who, yes, ranked over a [Lord], but was hardly the greatest noble in Ailendamus. True, there were [Barons] who had inspired fear in their enemies—great leaders in battle who were as dangerous as the Great Generals…"}
{"id":"01a0657e-133c-7e86-bbb3-f5a3b51cebec","chapterSlug":"rw8-36 H","paragraph":85,"wording":"[Baron]","event":"named","holderSlug":"baron-regalius","holderQuote":"So the [Baron] gave them a speech worthy of the occasion. He did not stutter. He did not look or sound bored—nor was he, and that was part of why he sounded good, even though he had said this a thousand times. When he addressed the knights-to-be, they looked up with a solemnity fitting for this occasion, nevermind they were not in the presence of their [King]."}
{"id":"01a0657e-133c-7bd4-b69e-e905a83fe782","chapterSlug":"rw8-36 H","paragraph":89,"wording":"[Baron]","event":"named","holderSlug":"baron-regalius","holderQuote":"A hundred [Knights]. The [Baron] was tired by the end of the four hour ceremony, and only his Skills and powers of speechcraft even made the moment awe-inspiring rather than tedious. Many nations might not knight so many [Knights] in a year!"}
{"id":"01a0657e-133c-73f8-9a58-775648f0859e","chapterSlug":"rw8-75","paragraph":467,"wording":"[Baron]","event":"named","holderQuote":"The listeners, the audience, turned and backed out of the way as the [Baron] strode through them."}
